anv: H.264 encode B frames as media-driver programs them (Xe2 VDEnc)

media-driver (AvcBasicFeature, AvcEncodeRounding, EncodeAvcVdencConstSettings) differs from what ANV programmed
for B-frame GOPs in four places, all now as media-driver does:
- VDENC_PIPE_MODE_SELECT IsRandomAccess for B pictures (randomAccess = CodingType == B_TYPE; Xe2);
- VDENC_CMD3 cost row of P pictures by GOP structure: 1 in a B GOP, 2 in an IP GOP (isIPGOP = GopRefDist == 1),
  from VkVideoEncodeH264RateControlInfoKHR::consecutiveBFrameCount (was always 2, the old TODO);
- inter rounding enabled in MFX_AVC_SLICE_STATE and VDENC_AVC_SLICE_STATE with the static BRC values
  (P 3, non-reference B 0, reference B 2; was disabled);
- reference B from StdVideoEncodeH264PictureInfo::flags.is_reference, not from pSetupReferenceSlot (FFmpeg passes a
  setup slot for non-reference B frames too): CMD3 row 3/4, CollocMVWREn and the Xe2 IMG_STATE ref row.
1080p60 VBR 3/6/12 Mbit/s, GOP 120, 2 B frames, Netflix Aerial: BD-rate against x264 medium +34.2% -> +18.9%
(PSNR-Y), +43.7% -> +25.4% (VMAF).

--- a/src/intel/vulkan/genX_cmd_video_enc.c
+++ b/src/intel/vulkan/genX_cmd_video_enc.c
@@ -528,6 +528,16 @@
    return vk_find_struct_const(enc_info->pNext, VIDEO_ENCODE_H264_PICTURE_INFO_KHR);
 }
 
+/* media-driver encode_avc_rounding.cpp / encode_avc_vdenc_const_settings.h (rounding inter, BRC): index
+ * isB ? (isRef ? 1 : 0) : (isIPGOP ? 3 : 2) into { 0, 2, 3, 3 } */
+static uint32_t
+anv_h264_round_inter(const VkVideoEncodeH264PictureInfoKHR *frame_info, uint32_t slice_type)
+{
+   if (slice_type == STD_VIDEO_H264_SLICE_TYPE_B)
+      return frame_info->pStdPictureInfo->flags.is_reference ? 2 : 0;
+   return 3;
+}
